@version 1
/// example: 229-vault-write-without-mut-invalid
/// level: 5
/// concept: FUNGI-VAULT-004 — vault write effect missing when flow mutates vault without declaring it
/// expected_diagnostics: FUNGI-VAULT-004
/// ai_rule: Every vault secure write must declare vault.write in the contract effects block. Missing the vault.write effect declaration emits FUNGI-VAULT-004.

vault secure {
  loginCount: Int {
    allow incrementLogin write
    allow getLoginCount  read
    audit required
  }
}

;; INVALID — vault.write effect is missing from the contract.
;; The flow mutates vault state but does not declare vault.write → FUNGI-VAULT-004.
;;
;; NOTE on what makes this a HONEST negative example: everything here except the missing
;; `vault.write` is CORRECT. The tier is `secure` because audit.write is a secure-tier effect,
;; and the boundary input is gated before it reaches a sink. Without that, the example emitted
;; FUNGI-TIER-001 and FUNGI-VALUESTATE-008 and never reached the defect it claims to teach —
;; a negative example must isolate exactly ONE fault, or the reader learns the wrong lesson.
secure flow incrementLogin(userId: String) -> Result<Bool, Error>
contract {
  intent "Increment the login counter (INVALID — missing vault.write in effects)"
  effects { audit.write }
}
{
  safe mut userId = validate.userId(userId)?

  ;; ⚠ THE DEFECT THIS EXAMPLE TEACHES CANNOT CURRENTLY BE WRITTEN.
  ;; `mut secure.loginCount = secure.loginCount + 1` is the syntax the governance verifier
  ;; documents (governance-verifier.ts:302) and that example 228 tells authors to use — but it
  ;; does NOT parse: parser.ts:1601 `parseMutDecl` consumes `mut`, ONE identifier, then expects
  ;; `=` immediately. There is no member-path production, so `mut secure.x` is unparseable by
  ;; construction. Attempting it emits two FUNGI-PARSE-001 alongside the intended FUNGI-VAULT-004.
  ;; Left un-written on purpose: an example must not teach syntax the compiler cannot accept.
  ;; Tracked as board #174. When the grammar lands, restore the write and this example becomes a
  ;; true single-fault negative.

  AuditLog.write({ event: "LoginAttempt", user: userId })
  return Ok(true)
}
